  "description": "<div><div style='font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'>The&nbsp;<a target='_blank' href='https://open.canada.ca/data/en/dataset/3ef8e8a9-8d05-4fea-a8bf-7f5023d2b6e1' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>National Ecological Framework for Canada&nbsp;<\/a>provides a consistent, national spatial framework that allows various ecosystems to be described, monitored and reported on. It provides standard ecological units that allow different jurisdictions and disciplines to use common communication and reporting, and a common ground to report on the state of the environment and the sustainability of ecosystems in Canada.<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'>The framework was developed between 1991 and 1999 by the Ecosystems Science Directorate, Environment Canada and the Center for Land and Biological Resources Research, Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada. Over 100 federal and provincial agencies, non-governmental organizations and private sector companies contributed to its development.&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit; font-size:16px;'>More information on the National Ecological Framework of Canada can be fund in the&nbsp;<a style='font-size:15px;' target='_blank' href='https://agriculture.canada.ca/atlas/data_donnees/nationalEcologicalFramework/supportdocument_documentdesupport/en/ISO_19131_National_Ecological_Framework_for_Canada_Data_Product_Specification.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Data Product Specification.<\/a><\/div><\/div><div>&nbsp;<\/div><p>The \u201cTerrestrial Ecoprovinces of Canada\u201d dataset provides representations of ecoprovinces. An ecoprovince is a subdivision of an ecozone and is characterized by major assemblages of structural or surface forms, faunal realms, and vegetation, hydrology, soil, and macro climate. For example, the Newfoundland ecoprovince (no. 6.4) is one of six ecoprovinces within the Boreal Shield Ecozone<br />&nbsp;<\/p><div>&nbsp;<\/div><div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><strong>Source:&nbsp;<\/strong><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><a style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size:15px;' target='_blank' href='https://open.canada.ca/data/en/dataset/98fa7335-fbfe-4289-9a0e-d6bf3874b424' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Terrestrial Ecoprovinces of Canada<\/a><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><a target='_blank' href='https://agriculture.canada.ca/atlas/data_donnees/nationalEcologicalFramework/supportdocument_documentdesupport/en/ISO_19131_National_Ecological_Framework_for_Canada_Data_Product_Specification.pdf' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Metadata<\/a><\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><strong>Update Frequency:&nbsp;<\/strong>As needed<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><strong>Related Layers:<\/strong><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><ul><li><a target='_blank' href='https://arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=501a40ba1aea4e3e96dab4715ce7d5af' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>Ecozones of Canada<\/a><\/li><li><a target='_blank' href='https://esricanada.maps.arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=ee462b0692cc4005aefee69dc44f010d' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>EcoRegions of Canada<\/a><\/li><li><a target='_blank' href='https://arcgis.com/home/item.html?id=47d35e24ab3f4349b34521c485c37ad1' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>EcoDistricts of Canada<\/a><\/li><\/ul><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'>&nbsp;<\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><div style='font-family:inherit;'><strong>Contact Information:<\/strong><\/div><div style='font-family:inherit;'><ul><li>For inquiries on the data contact&nbsp;Agriculture and Agri-Food Canada (aafc.cansis-siscan.aac@agr.gc.ca)<\/li><li>For inquires regarding the service, please leave a comment below<\/li><\/ul><\/div><\/div><\/div><\/div>",
